{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>תועבת</b>, <b>רצון</b>, <b>חמת</b>, <b>באור</b>, <b>קנה</b> — five [words] linked together. [verses 12–16] Each of the kings loves." "Melaket [late lessons?] — it is the rain. And likewise its interpretation: the kings are fit to abhor a doer of wickedness, for on account of the justice they do their throne will be established, and they will accept the speaker of justice, that is, a speaker of faithful uprightness the king will love, for his wrath is like the wrath of angels of death, who put the wicked to death suddenly."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:09.893001079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}